# Static site rules

## Architecture

This is a static HTML/CSS/JS website.

Use existing files and patterns unless explicitly told otherwise.

## HTML

When editing HTML:

- preserve semantic structure
- keep one clear H1 per page
- preserve existing navigation and footer structure
- use existing CSS classes where practical
- use relative links consistently
- include useful alt text for meaningful images
- avoid empty placeholder sections on the public site

## CSS

When editing CSS:

- use existing variables and design tokens when available
- avoid duplicating styles unnecessarily
- avoid large visual redesigns unless requested
- keep mobile behavior in mind
- do not create one-off styling if an existing pattern works

## JavaScript

When editing JavaScript:

- keep it vanilla JS
- avoid adding dependencies
- preserve existing mobile nav, FAQ accordion, scroll behavior, and card behavior
- avoid broad rewrites
- comment only when it helps clarify non-obvious logic

## No build step

Do not add a build step.

Do not suggest npm commands unless package.json exists and the user specifically asks to change architecture.